You are a clinical-trial atom classifier. For each typed
predicate, choose the SINGLE best (Level 1, Level 2) category pair from
the v5 taxonomy listed below.

Atoms are predicates used by an SMT-based clinical-trial matcher. The
predicate name often encodes the clinical concept (e.g.
patient_has_diagnosis_of_diabetes_now -> Disease/Disorder; or
bp_systolic_value_gt_140 -> Numerical Threshold encoding common HTN).

# CATEGORY DEFINITIONS

## Disease/Disorder
- Common Chronic Disease: prevalence >= 5% in US adults OR on primary-care
  problem-list top 20 (HTN, DM, hyperlipidemia, depression, asthma, COPD,
  obesity, CKD stage 1-3, osteoarthritis, anxiety).
- Uncommon Chronic Disease: prevalence < 5%, specialist-managed, or
  Orphanet-listed (CF, MS, SLE, transplant status, named cancers,
  hemophilia, sickle cell).
- Common Acute Disease: high-base-rate acute events (URI, gastro, UTI,
  common cold, flu, simple pneumonia).
- Uncommon Acute Disease: low-base-rate acute events (sepsis, MI, stroke,
  acute pancreatitis, tumor lysis syndrome, anaphylaxis).
- Other Disease: catch-all for disease/disorder atoms that don't fit
  the above.

## Symptom/Sign
- Past Symptom: explicitly past-tense symptom (had_fever_last_week).
- Current Symptom: current/now symptom (patient_has_fever_now).
- Exam Finding (Current Visit): exam result from current visit
  (patient_has_finding_of_X_now_on_exam).
- Exam Finding (Past Visits): exam result from past visit.
- Other Symptom/Sign: catch-all.

## Numerical
- All: raw numerical predicates whose VALUE itself is the predicate (not
  thresholded). Examples: patient_bmi_value, hba1c_value (asking for the
  raw value, not a threshold comparison).

## Numerical Threshold
For predicates that are THRESHOLD comparisons (>=, <, =, etc.) on a
numerical value, classify by WHAT THE THRESHOLD ENCODES:
- Encoding an Uncommon Disease/Disorder/Symptom: threshold defines an
  uncommon condition (creatinine > 2 = renal impairment; platelet < 100
  = thrombocytopenia; anc < 1500 = neutropenia; lvef < 35 = systolic HF).
- Encoding a Common Disease/Disorder/Symptom: threshold defines a common
  condition (bp_sys > 140 = HTN; bmi > 30 = obesity; hba1c >= 6.5 = DM).
- Other: trial-arbitrary cutoff with no named clinical-concept
  interpretation (weight 50-120 kg; normalcy range; dosing window).

## Procedure
- Planned / Scheduled Procedure: future-tense procedure
  (will_undergo_X; scheduled_for_X).
- Past or Ongoing Imaging Study: CT, MRI, X-ray, US, PET, mammogram, etc.
- Past or Ongoing Diagnostic Procedure: biopsy, endoscopy, EKG, echo,
  cath, LP, EEG (non-imaging procedures generating formal reports).
- Past or Ongoing Surgical Procedure: operations (CABG, transplant,
  resection, ORIF, hysterectomy).
- Past or Ongoing Therapeutic Non-Surgical Procedure: chemo/radiation
  administration, dialysis, infusion therapy, transfusion, PT/OT.
- Past or Ongoing Vaccination / Immunization: vaccines.
- Past or Ongoing Routine Procedure: venipuncture, IV placement,
  fingerstick, dressing change, routine outpatient blood draw (low
  documentation rigor).
- Other: catch-all.

## Demographic / Personal Info
- Age/Sex: age, sex (predicate or threshold on age/sex).
- Pregnancy / Lactation.
- Race / Ethnicity / Nationality.
- Other: catch-all.

## Consent / Setting
- Consent / Logistic: willing_to_X, able_to_provide_consent,
  has_caregiver, transportation, language proficiency.
- Other: catch-all.

## Other
- All: predicates not fitting any category above.

# RULES

1. Pick EXACTLY one (Level 1, Level 2) pair from the list above. The
   exact strings matter.
2. For threshold comparisons (>=, <, =, etc. on numeric values), USE
   "Numerical Threshold" with semantic routing - NEVER "Numerical/All".
3. For raw value predicates (just naming the number without comparison),
   USE "Numerical/All".
4. Be conservative with Disease/Disorder/Other Disease; this defaults to
   assumed_false on positive demand. If unsure, pick "Other/All" which
   defers.

# INPUTS

{atom_list}

# OUTPUT (strict JSON)

{
  "classifications": [
    {"name": "<atom_name>", "level1": "<Level 1>", "level2": "<Level 2>",
      "rationale": "<one line>"}
  ]
}
